import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart' show BuildContext, Color;
import 'package:magic/magic.dart';

/// **Semantic Token Alias Convention**
///
/// [MagicStarterTokens] provides the default light+dark alias map for the
/// magic_starter component system. Every component resolves colors through
/// these semantic role names rather than palette utilities directly, so a
/// single `DESIGN.md` override (generated by `design:sync`) can re-skin the
/// entire starter kit without touching component code.
///
/// ## Alias Key Convention
///
/// Alias keys follow the CSS-property-prefix convention:
///
/// - **Background roles** use `bg-{role}`: `bg-surface`, `bg-primary`,
///   `bg-destructive`, etc. A component writes `className: 'bg-surface p-4'`
///   and the alias expander replaces the bare `bg-surface` token before the
///   wind parser sees it.
/// - **Text / foreground roles** use `text-{role}`: `text-fg`, `text-fg-muted`,
///   `text-on-primary`, etc.
/// - **Border color roles** use `border-color-{role}`: `border-color-border`,
///   `border-color-border-subtle`. Note: the bare `border` Tailwind utility
///   (add a 1 px border) is separate and unaffected.
///
/// ## Alias Values
///
/// Each value is a wind className string containing exactly two tokens:
///
/// - one bare palette utility (applied in **light** mode), and
/// - one `dark:`-prefixed palette utility (applied in **dark** mode).
///
/// Example: `'bg-white dark:bg-gray-950'`
///
/// The `primary-*` shade references (`bg-primary-600`, `text-primary-600`,
/// etc.) resolve against the consumer-supplied `primary` [MaterialColor] in
/// [WindThemeData.colors] — this map never hardcodes the brand color.
///
/// ## Design:sync Target
///
/// Steps 20-21 (`design:sync`) will later generate a replacement map from a
/// `DESIGN.md` file using arbitrary-hex values
/// (`'bg-[#f9f9ff] dark:bg-[#0f1419]'`). The key set in [defaultAliases] is
/// the **stable contract** that the generated map must satisfy; do not rename
/// keys without coordinating the `design:sync` emitter.
///
/// ## Semantic Roles
///
/// The 17 semantic roles and their key prefixes:
///
/// | Role | Alias key |
/// |------|-----------|
/// | surface | `bg-surface` |
/// | surface-container | `bg-surface-container` |
/// | surface-container-high | `bg-surface-container-high` |
/// | fg | `text-fg` |
/// | fg-muted | `text-fg-muted` |
/// | fg-disabled | `text-fg-disabled` |
/// | primary | `bg-primary` |
/// | on-primary | `text-on-primary` |
/// | primary-container | `bg-primary-container` |
/// | accent | `bg-accent` |
/// | border | `border-color-border` |
/// | border-subtle | `border-color-border-subtle` |
/// | destructive | `bg-destructive` |
/// | on-destructive | `text-on-destructive` |
/// | destructive-container | `bg-destructive-container` |
/// | success | `bg-success` |
/// | warning | `bg-warning` |
///
/// Beside them sit the soft tints the support screens use: `bg-warning-soft`,
/// `bg-success-soft`, `bg-ai-soft` (each with its `text-*-soft-foreground`) and
/// the `border-ai` accent edge.
///
/// ## Usage
///
/// ```dart
/// final windTheme = WindThemeData(
///   colors: {'primary': myBrandColor},
///   aliases: MagicStarterTokens.defaultAliases,
/// );
/// ```
///
/// In a component:
///
/// ```dart
/// WDiv(
///   className: 'bg-surface text-fg border border-[1px] rounded-lg p-4',
///   child: WText('Hello', className: 'text-fg'),
/// )
/// ```
///
/// ## Roles the map does not ship
///
/// `text-destructive` is not a key in [defaultAliases], yet a host may define
/// it (typically as its brand red). [role] resolves such a token against
/// the active theme: the host's own definition when it has one, the red text
/// pair otherwise.
///
/// `text-on-success` and `text-on-warning` are the same kind of role: the text
/// and icon colour that reads on `bg-success` and `bg-warning`. A host that
/// defines its own fills defines these beside them (a host whose dark fills are
/// light needs dark text there). Without them [role] answers with near-black,
/// which reads on the stock fills, and [readableOn] measures the fill a
/// component paints and picks white or near-black by contrast instead.
final class MagicStarterTokens {
  MagicStarterTokens._();

  /// Fallback palette pairs for semantic roles that are NOT keys in
  /// [defaultAliases].
  ///
  /// `text-primary` resolves directly against the `primary` colour and is always
  /// available, so its fallback is only a safety net. `text-destructive` has no
  /// canonical alias (the contract ships `bg-destructive` / `text-on-destructive`
  /// only), so it falls back to the red text pair.
  ///
  /// `text-on-success` and `text-on-warning` are the text and icon colours that
  /// read on `bg-success` and `bg-warning`. The contract ships the two fills but
  /// no such roles, so a host that defines its own fills defines them beside
  /// them (a host whose dark fills are light needs dark text there). The pair
  /// here is only what [role] answers with no fill to measure: the near-black
  /// `gray-950`, which reads on the STOCK fills (green and amber, 600 in light
  /// and 500 in dark) at about 6:1 to 9:1 where white reads at 3.3:1 and 3.2:1.
  /// [readableOn] is what a component uses when it has a build context: it
  /// measures the fill instead of assuming the stock one.
  static const Map<String, String> _roleFallbacks = {
    'text-primary': 'text-primary',
    'text-destructive': 'text-red-600 dark:text-red-400',
    'text-on-success': 'text-gray-950 dark:text-gray-950',
    'text-on-warning': 'text-gray-950 dark:text-gray-950',
  };

  /// Resolves a semantic role [token] against [theme].
  ///
  /// Returns the bare [token] when [theme] defines the role, either as an alias
  /// key (`bg-surface`, `text-fg`, `border-color-border`, ...) or through its
  /// backing colour in [WindThemeData.colors] (`bg-primary` -> `primary`), so
  /// the surface re-skins with the host palette. Otherwise returns the shipped
  /// [defaultAliases] value, then the built-in fallback pair, so the surface
  /// stays visible instead of resolving to a token wind drops silently.
  ///
  /// A null [theme] means no `WindTheme` ancestor: the fallback applies.
  static String role(WindThemeData? theme, String token) {
    if (theme != null && _themeDefines(theme, token)) {
      return token;
    }

    return defaultAliases[token] ?? _roleFallbacks[token] ?? token;
  }

  /// The text class that reads on the [fill] a component paints, for the
  /// on-colour [role] of that fill.
  ///
  /// A role the host defines is returned as it is: the host's word is final,
  /// poor contrast included. Otherwise the fallback cannot assume the stock
  /// fill, because a host may redefine `bg-success` as a dark green and define
  /// no `text-on-success`: near-black on it is about 3:1. So the fill is resolved
  /// from the theme in the current brightness and the better of white and the
  /// near-black `gray-950` by WCAG contrast is returned (`text-white` or
  /// `text-gray-950`, one mode at a time; the context depends on the theme, so
  /// a brightness change rebuilds it). On the stock fills that is the near-black
  /// they have always had here. A translucent fill is measured over the
  /// `bg-surface` it is painted on, since its own colour alone says nothing about
  /// what the text sits on. With no fill to measure (the theme resolves [fill]
  /// or, for a translucent one, `bg-surface` to nothing) the answer is [role]'s
  /// fallback pair.
  static String readableOn(
    BuildContext context, {
    required String fill,
    required String role,
  }) {
    final WindThemeData? theme = WindTheme.maybeDataOf(context);
    if (theme != null && _themeDefines(theme, role)) {
      return role;
    }

    final Color? fillColour = _opaqueFill(fill, context);
    final Color? light = WindParser.parse('text-white', context).color;
    final Color? dark = WindParser.parse('text-gray-950', context).color;
    if (fillColour == null || light == null || dark == null) {
      return MagicStarterTokens.role(theme, role);
    }

    return _contrast(light, fillColour) >= _contrast(dark, fillColour)
        ? 'text-white'
        : 'text-gray-950';
  }

  /// The colour [fill] paints, laid over `bg-surface` when it is translucent, or
  /// null when the theme resolves it (or the surface it needs) to nothing.
  static Color? _opaqueFill(String fill, BuildContext context) {
    final Color? colour = WindParser.parse(fill, context).decoration?.color;
    if (colour == null || colour.a >= 1) {
      return colour;
    }

    final Color? surface = WindParser.parse(
      'bg-surface',
      context,
    ).decoration?.color;

    return surface == null ? null : Color.alphaBlend(colour, surface);
  }

  /// WCAG contrast ratio of two colours, from their relative luminance.
  static double _contrast(Color a, Color b) {
    final double la = a.computeLuminance();
    final double lb = b.computeLuminance();

    return (la > lb ? la + 0.05 : lb + 0.05) /
        (la > lb ? lb + 0.05 : la + 0.05);
  }

  static bool _themeDefines(WindThemeData theme, String token) {
    if (theme.aliases.containsKey(token)) {
      return true;
    }

    final colorKey = _backingColorKey(token);
    return colorKey != null && theme.colors.containsKey(colorKey);
  }

  /// Strips the CSS-property prefix off a semantic [token] to recover its
  /// backing colour key (`border-color-border` -> `border`, `bg-primary` ->
  /// `primary`, `text-fg` -> `fg`), or `null` when the token carries no known
  /// prefix.
  static String? _backingColorKey(String token) {
    for (final prefix in const ['border-color-', 'bg-', 'text-']) {
      if (token.startsWith(prefix)) {
        return token.substring(prefix.length);
      }
    }

    return null;
  }

  /// The default semantic alias map providing light+dark token pairs for all
  /// 17 semantic roles used by the magic_starter component system.
  ///
  /// Keys follow the `bg-{role}` / `text-{role}` / `border-color-{role}`
  /// convention so they match the unprefixed tokens used in component
  /// className strings. See the class-level documentation for the full
  /// key-to-role mapping table.
  ///
  /// The `primary-*` shade references resolve against the consumer-supplied
  /// `primary` [MaterialColor] in [WindThemeData.colors]; the brand color is
  /// never hardcoded here.
  static const Map<String, String> defaultAliases = {
    // -- Surface roles (bg- prefix) -----------------------------------------

    /// Main app surface: page and modal backgrounds.
    'bg-surface': 'bg-white dark:bg-gray-950',

    /// Slightly elevated container: cards, panels.
    'bg-surface-container': 'bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900',

    /// More elevated container: nested cards, input backgrounds.
    'bg-surface-container-high': 'bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800',

    // -- Foreground roles (text- prefix) ------------------------------------

    /// Primary body text.
    'text-fg': 'text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50',

    /// Secondary / muted text: labels, captions.
    'text-fg-muted': 'text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400',

    /// Disabled text: placeholder, inactive labels.
    'text-fg-disabled': 'text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-600',

    // -- Primary roles ------------------------------------------------------

    /// Primary action background: buttons, active states.
    /// Resolves against the consumer-supplied `primary` color in WindThemeData.
    'bg-primary': 'bg-primary-600 dark:bg-primary-500',

    /// Text / icon on top of the primary background.
    'text-on-primary': 'text-white dark:text-white',

    /// Light tinted container for primary-adjacent surfaces.
    'bg-primary-container': 'bg-primary-100 dark:bg-primary-900',

    // -- Accent role --------------------------------------------------------

    /// Secondary accent background for decorative highlights (default: indigo).
    'bg-accent': 'bg-indigo-600 dark:bg-indigo-500',

    // -- Border color roles (border-color- prefix) --------------------------
    //
    // Note: these control border COLOR only. The `border` / `border-{width}`
    // Tailwind utilities that add border-width are separate bare tokens and
    // are not affected by these aliases.

    /// Default border and divider color.
    'border-color-border': 'border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700',

    /// Subtle divider, less prominent than `border-color-border`.
    'border-color-border-subtle': 'border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800',

    // -- Semantic state roles (bg- / text- prefix) --------------------------

    /// Destructive / danger action background.
    'bg-destructive': 'bg-red-600 dark:bg-red-500',

    /// Text / icon on top of the destructive background.
    'text-on-destructive': 'text-white dark:text-white',

    /// Light tinted container for destructive-adjacent surfaces.
    'bg-destructive-container': 'bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-900',

    /// Success / positive confirmation background.
    'bg-success': 'bg-green-600 dark:bg-green-500',

    /// Warning / caution background.
    'bg-warning': 'bg-amber-600 dark:bg-amber-500',

    // -- AI content roles ---------------------------------------------------
    //
    // Mark content an assistant wrote. Shared views may use these without a
    // host-only token; a host theme that defines the same keys (uptizm does)
    // supplies its own map and wins.

    /// Soft violet container for AI-authored content: replies, summaries.
    'bg-ai-soft': 'bg-violet-100 dark:bg-violet-900',

    /// Text / icon on top of the `bg-ai-soft` container.
    'text-ai-soft-foreground': 'text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-200',

    /// Accent edge of AI-authored content: the left rule of an AI bubble.
    'border-ai': 'border-violet-500 dark:border-violet-400',

    // -- Soft state tints ---------------------------------------------------
    //
    // The quiet counterpart of `bg-warning` / `bg-success`: a tinted fill with
    // its own text, for status pills that sit in a list and must not shout.
    // A host map that defines the same keys wins.

    /// Soft amber container: "a teammate is answering".
    'bg-warning-soft': 'bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900',

    /// Text / icon on top of the `bg-warning-soft` container.
    'text-warning-soft-foreground': 'text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-200',

    /// Soft green container: "resolved".
    'bg-success-soft': 'bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900',

    /// Text / icon on top of the `bg-success-soft` container.
    'text-success-soft-foreground': 'text-green-800 dark:text-green-200',
  };
}
